          "<strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">W:</span></strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\"> OK everyone, before you head out to the factory floor this morning to start your </span><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">shifts</span><span style=\"color: #000000;\">, have a brief announcement. As most of you know, </span><strong><span style=\"color: #00B050;\">(1)</span></strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\"> </span><span style=\"color: #000000;\">the new conveyor belt is now installed and up and running</span><span style=\"color: #000000;\">. </span><strong><span style=\"color: #00B050;\">(2)</span></strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\"> </span><span style=\"color: #000000;\">This new conveyor belt is very similar to the </span><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">older</span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"> model, except it&#x27;s twice as fast as the old one</span><span style=\"color: #000000;\">. This means that our factory can now move </span><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">double</span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"> the number of units per hour. Clearly, this is a big improvement in production </span><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">speed</span><span style=\"color: #000000;\">. However, it could also be a challenge for us to watch out for production errors. So</span>,<strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\"> </span></strong><strong><span style=\"color: #00B050;\">(3)</span></strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\"> </span><span style=\"color: #000000;\">you&#x27;re all required to watch a short </span><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">training</span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"> video this morning before starting work</span><span style=\"color: #000000;\">. </span>"
        ]
