          "<strong>W:</strong> <strong><span style=\"color: #00B050;\">(1)</span></strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\"> </span>This is Health on the Go, a weekly <span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">broadcast </span>that gives you advice about your eating habits. Today we&#x27;re talking about salt. Who&#x27;s heard that salt is not good for you? Well... <strong><span style=\"color: #00B050;\">(2)</span></strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\"> </span>this negative view of salt is surprising because it&#x27;s simply not true. You actually do need some salt in your diet to remain <span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">healthy</span>. But remember. salt occurs naturally in most foods, so you don&#x27;t need to add extra salt to your diet. In fact, even",
          "fruits and vegetables <span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">contain</span> salt. <strong><span style=\"color: #00B050;\">(3)</span></strong><strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\"> </span></strong>I know you&#x27;re all interested in trying more recipes that use fruits and vegetables. We&#x27;ll be talking about that on next week&#x27;s broadcast."
