            "id": 3,
            "slide_index": 315,
            "question": "<strong>Question 03.</strong> What does the speaker ask the listeners do?<br><strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">",
            "choices": {
              "A": "Get approval for travel",
              "B": "Review a revised budget",
              "C": "Meet with some customers",
              "D": "</span></strong>Provide feedback on a schedule"
            },
            "answer": "C"
          }
        ],
        "transcript": [
          "<strong>W</strong>: Good morning. The main focus of today&#x27;s meeting is our bus company&#x27;s quarterly earnings. Overall, we&#x27;re doing well, but <strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">(1)</span></strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\"> </span>there has been a noticeable drop in ticket sales on routes to Cooper City. Cooper City was once a major tourist destination, but since several museums closed in the historic district, fewer passengers choose to go there. This&#x27;ll now be the third quarter in a row of a steady decline in ticket purchases, so <strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">(2)</span></strong> I think it best to reduce the number of bus trips to that location to just one a day. <strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">(3)</span></strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\"> </span>I&#x27;ve created an updated schedule that reflects this change. Please look it over and let me know what you think."
        ]
      },
      {
        "set_index": 6,
        "audio": "media47.mp3",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": 1,
            "slide_index": 318,
            "question": "<strong>Question 01. </strong>Why is a change being made?",
            "choices": {
              "A": "To improve efficiency",
              "B": "To follow a safety procedure",
              "C": "To make some repairs",
              "D": "To prepare for new hires"
            },
            "answer": "A"
          },
          {
            "id": 2,
            "slide_index": 320,
            "question": "<strong>Question 02. </strong>Look at the graphic. Where are the new shelves located?",
            "choices": {
              "A": "Area 1",
              "B": "Area 2",
              "C": "Area 3",
              "D": "Area 4"
            },
            "answer": "D"
          },
          {
            "id": 3,
            "slide_index": 322,
            "question": "<strong>Question 03. </strong>What does the speaker say listeners can find in the office?",
            "choices": {
              "A": "Some work badges",
              "B": "Some equipment manuals",
              "C": "A sign-up sheet",
              "D": "An employee handbook"
            },
            "answer": "C"
          }
        ],
        "transcript": [
          "<strong>W:</strong> Good morning. <strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">(1)</span></strong> I called this staff meeting to discuss the reorganization of our warehouse. On average, each of you spends five minutes finding the products you need to complete an order for shipment. But, I think we can get that number down by making the most popular items easier to find. Here&#x27;s a map of the warehouse. <strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">(2)</span></strong> I&#x27;ve added some new shelving units between the order station and the employee lounge. That&#x27;s where we&#x27;ll place our high-demand products. Now, I&#x27;ll need some people to help rearrange the inventory. So, <strong><span style=\"color: #FF0000;\">(3)</span></strong> if you&#x27;re willing to work a few extra hours, please add your name to the sign-up sheet in my office."
        ]
      }
    ]
